From b28a832fefaaefbeb2ad0dfd51731edaee38c8cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Wloga <michal.wloga@envirosolutions.pl>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:04:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] [server] Speed up the conversion of WMS images to 8
 bits PNG

- The closest color of the color table is searched with the distances to
  all the colors calculated at once, and kept in a direct mapped cache
  instead of a hash. The result is the same as with
  QImage::convertToFormat() called with a color table, which is tested.
- The color boxes of the median cut are stored in a vector instead of
  a list which allocates every item, and sorted with inlined comparisons.

A 1024x768 map with three vector layers is returned 13% faster as
image/png; mode=8bit.

